---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { PROJECT_LINKS, repoFile, SITE } from "../config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Docs"
  description="How Servotab calibrates method to repository risk, evidence, and the requested outcome."
>
  <PageIntro
    index="01 / Docs"
    title="Method stays subordinate to the work."
    description="Servotab is a skills-only engineering method layer for Codex. It calibrates how much process a repository task receives without taking ownership away from the task, the repo, or the user."
  />

  <section class="content-band" aria-labelledby="get-started-heading">
    <div class="shell content-layout">
      <p class="section-index">Get started</p>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <h2 id="get-started-heading">Add the public plugin. Or inspect the source candidate.</h2>
        <p>
          Servotab is publicly available in the official OpenAI Plugins Directory.{" "}
          <a href={PROJECT_LINKS.pluginDirectory}>Open the Servotab listing</a> to add the
          published plugin. The repository route below installs the separate
          {" "}<code>{SITE.version}</code> source candidate for inspection or maintainer testing;
          it is not a readback of the currently published directory payload.
        </p>

        <div class="quickstart-grid">
          <article>
            <span class="rail-label">01 / source checkout</span>
            <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/IndelibleVivi/servotab.git
cd servotab
codex plugin marketplace add .
codex plugin add servotab@personal</code></pre>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="rail-label">02 / ask</span>
            <div class="quickstart-example">
              <span>ordinary language</span>
              <p>Fix the stale-cursor regression, identify the violated invariant, repair the canonical source, and run the focused suite.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="quickstart-example">
              <span>precise control</span>
              <p><code>$review</code> inspect this diff and report only verified, actionable P0–P2 findings.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <h3>Confirm the current install.</h3>
        <p>
          Open a fresh Codex task or process after installation, then read back the
          configured marketplace package instead of assuming the active process refreshed:
        </p>
        <pre><code>codex plugin list --marketplace personal</code></pre>
        <p>
          The receipt should show <code>servotab@personal</code> as{" "}
          <code>installed, enabled</code> at version <code>{SITE.version}</code>. On
          2026-08-31 this source-checkout route and fresh-process router discovery were
          verified on macOS with <code>codex-cli 0.147.0</code>. That is an observed
          compatibility receipt, not a guessed minimum-version guarantee.
        </p>

        <h3>One implicit router. Twelve explicit shortcuts.</h3>
        <p>
          Describe ordinary repository work normally. Servotab may keep a clear change
          direct or load one relevant method when risk or uncertainty warrants it. Use
          names such as <code>$review</code>, <code>$tdd</code>, or <code>$spec-chain</code>{" "}
          when you want precise control; the twelve method leaves are not implicit workflows.
        </p>

        <h3>A skills-only product boundary.</h3>
        <p>
          Servotab adds no Servotab account, backend, database, telemetry service, or
          network endpoint, and the publisher does not receive repository contents through
          the plugin. Codex and any repositories, browsers, terminals, tools, or external
          services it uses remain governed by their own permissions and data practices.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band" aria-labelledby="working-model-heading">
    <div class="shell content-layout">
      <p class="section-index">Working model</p>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <h2 id="working-model-heading">One router. A bounded set of methods.</h2>
        <p>
          Ordinary work begins in natural language. Servotab first asks whether
          the task is already clear, local, and reversible. If it is, Codex should
          work directly. If the task carries material uncertainty or risk, Servotab
          selects the method that addresses that specific pressure.
        </p>

        <div class="direct-method-rail">
          <article>
            <span class="rail-label">clear / local</span>
            <h3>Stay direct</h3>
            <p>Inspect only what matters, make the coherent change, and verify the affected behavior.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="rail-label">uncertain / risky</span>
            <h3>Invoke method</h3>
            <p>Add design, planning, debugging, testing, review, isolation, delegation, or closure only where it protects the outcome.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band" aria-labelledby="task-shapes-heading">
    <div class="shell content-layout">
      <p class="section-index">Task shapes</p>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <h2 id="task-shapes-heading">Proportionate, in concrete terms.</h2>
        <p>
          The method depth changes with the pressure in the work—not with a fixed ritual.
          These three shapes mirror the public behavior cases maintained in the repository.
        </p>

        <div class="step-list">
          <div class="step-row">
            <span>01</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Change one empty-state string.</h3>
              <p>One file, the narrowest meaningful check, no plan, and no delegation overhead.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-row">
            <span>02</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Repair a stale-cursor regression.</h3>
              <p>Reproduce the failure, locate the consistency-window invariant, repair canonical source, and run the focused regression suite.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-row">
            <span>03</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Plan from an approved specification.</h3>
              <p>Retain every requirement and dependency boundary; a convenient first tranche does not redefine completion.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="evidence-link">
          <a href={repoFile("evals/README.md")}>Inspect the public behavior-evidence contract</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band" aria-labelledby="sequence-heading">
    <div class="shell content-layout">
      <p class="section-index">Sequence</p>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <h2 id="sequence-heading">Tab first. Response second. Receipt. Stop.</h2>
        <p>
          The motion grammar describes product behavior: intervention is small,
          causal, and finite. Servotab does not add ambient “thinking” animation
          or keep a task inside a process after the evidence has settled.
        </p>

        <div class="step-list">
          <div class="step-row">
            <span>01</span>
            <div><h3>The base already exists.</h3><p>The requested task and repository remain the primary surface.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-row">
            <span>02</span>
            <div><h3>A method attaches locally.</h3><p>A bounded technique appears where it can materially change confidence or direction.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-row">
            <span>03</span>
            <div><h3>The larger work responds.</h3><p>The plan, implementation, diagnosis, or review changes in a way proportionate to the risk.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-row">
            <span>04</span>
            <div><h3>Fresh evidence settles the state.</h3><p>A named check or observed result supports the claim, and then the method stops.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band content-band-ink" aria-labelledby="boundaries-heading">
    <div class="shell content-layout">
      <p class="section-index">Boundaries</p>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <h2 id="boundaries-heading">What Servotab does not claim.</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>It does not replace the user’s prompt, repository instructions, permissions, or Git decisions.</li>
          <li>A log, review, plan, or generated artifact may inform the work; it does not authorize itself.</li>
          <li>It does not make every task follow one mandatory end-to-end workflow.</li>
          <li>It does not treat a green build as proof of deployment, runtime activation, or owner acceptance.</li>
          <li>It does not turn an explicit complete request into a scaffold, placeholder, or unnamed partial result.</li>
          <li>The public directory listing proves availability; it does not make Servotab an official OpenAI product or transfer repository authority to the directory surface.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band" aria-labelledby="availability-heading">
    <div class="shell content-layout">
      <p class="section-index">Status &amp; evidence</p>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <h2 id="availability-heading">Verified to the boundary we can prove.</h2>
        <p>
          The current <code>{SITE.version}</code> source candidate is generated from canonical
          method and icon sources into an exact 69-file plugin package. Public checks cover
          source/generated sync, skill validation, manifest freshness, package self-tests,
          public-tree audit, Python compilation, website motion behavior, and the production
          build. Those gates establish source and package consistency plus the checked UI
          behavior; they do not prove behavior on every machine or publication of this newer
          candidate.
        </p>
        <p>
          The <a href={PROJECT_LINKS.pluginDirectory}>official Servotab listing</a> is live.
          The current <code>{SITE.version}</code> repository candidate strengthens the router,
          design, execution, verification, and race-safe motion contracts while retaining the
          per-skill icons. It remains distinct from that published payload until Faye manually
          submits and OpenAI publishes the update. GitHub release availability is recorded on the repository Releases page.
          The same repository preserves earlier Softpowers commits, release records,
          licensing history, and provenance without relabelling those historical versions.
        </p>
        <p class="evidence-link">
          <a href={PROJECT_LINKS.pluginDirectory}>Official listing</a>{" · "}
          <a href={PROJECT_LINKS.source}>Source</a>{" · "}
          <a href={repoFile("CHANGELOG.md")}>Changelog</a>{" · "}
          <a href={repoFile("docs/current-state.md")}>Current state</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
